{
 "about": "DOLORES, the Separation Chair's assistant: machine-generated speech (VoxCPM2, a voice designed from a written description, through a 30 Hz ring modulator and a small-speaker chain; see README.md). One entry per line; ticks are the chair operation's (ChairTimeline).",
 "requirements": [
  "The client picks the English or the Portuguese event from its own language setting: Minecraft.getInstance().getLanguageManager().getSelected() starting with \"pt\" plays the pt event, anything else the en event. The server never chooses; it sends which line (and the chair) to every player tracking the chair.",
  "Sound category VOICE (the Voice/Speech slider), so players can turn DOLORES down on her own.",
  "Positional at the chair block centre, mono, volume 1.0, pitch 1.0 (never randomised), linear attenuation, range 16 blocks.",
  "Voiced during the operation: start, gas, scan, jar, then done or oopsie. cut and privacy have voiced_in_operation false: text only during the operation (their files are kept, unused).",
  "Each language has its own spacing: start tick = trigger tick + en.offset_ticks or pt.offset_ticks (the language the client plays). A line never overlaps the next line's start; a new DOLORES line from the same chair stops the one still playing.",
  "The patient hears the *_muffled event for voiced lines marked muffled (gas, scan, jar); everyone else hears the clear event.",
  "Ducking: a chair effect from the same chair that starts inside a line's window plays at the listed dB (volume x 10^(dB/20)) for that client; the cut, the latch at 100, the barrier latch, the clamp and the ding never duck.",
  "Refusal and blade lines: at most one per chair every 60 ticks, and the same refusal at most once per sitting.",
  "Off switch: a client config doloresVoice (default true); off means the payload is ignored and the text stays.",
  "Subtitles: register the subtitle key on each event; the action-bar line keeps the full written text."
 ],
 "category": "voice",
 "range_blocks": 16,
 "volume": 1.0,
 "pitch": 1.0,
 "stream": false,
 "loudness": "every clear file M max -24 (vanilla villager idle1 -24.1); muffled files 6 dB under (-30); peak <= -1 dBFS",
 "muffle": {
  "lowpass_hz": 1400,
  "order": 2,
  "gain_db": -6.0
 },
